handle it in play by post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 03-14-2015, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:12:11-07:00","id":440850,"title":"","content":"I probably shouldn't join another play by post game, but I do have a First Age Chosen of Battles Concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:21:12-07:00","id":440852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth?p=440850#post440850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably shouldn't join another play by post game, but I do have a First Age Chosen of Battles Concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds interesting but it's not gonna be a first age game but your character could work in one of the scenario I thought about can you tell me a bit more about it ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:40:18-07:00","id":440869,"title":"","content":"I guess it would depend on how old the characters are. My character concept requires her to be born in First Age. (Before Arcane Fate and when Dragon Blooded blood lines were more pure)<br /> <br /> The character was born into a Dragon Blooded Gent and was Fated to Exalt as a Sidereal. Which means that she was a mortal, not a Dragon blood. Which meant that Gent's bloodline wasn't a pure as they portrayed. So it was a large scandal for the Gent when the Sidereals claimed her as an infant.<br /> <br /> While her parents were ashamed of her, her Dragon blooded brothers and sisters see the advantage of having a Celestial exalt in the family. She gets a lot of crap from other Celestial Exalts because of her close relationship with the Dragon blooded. They call her the Dragon Star because of it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-14-2015, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:09:20-07:00","id":440884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth?p=440869#post440869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it would depend on how old the characters are. My character concept requires her to be born in First Age. (Before Arcane Fate and when Dragon Blooded blood lines were more pure)<br /> <br /> The character was born into a Dragon Blooded Gent and was Fated to Exalt as a Sidereal. Which means that she was a mortal, not a Dragon blood. Which meant that Gent's bloodline wasn't a pure as they portrayed. So it was a large scandal for the Gent when the Sidereals claimed her as an infant.<br /> <br /> While her parents were ashamed of her, her Dragon blooded brothers and sisters see the advantage of having a Celestial exalt in the family. She gets a lot of crap from other Celestial Exalts because of her close relationship with the Dragon blooded. They call her the Dragon Star because of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>the basic idea I had was experienced exalted coming out of stasis after escaping the madness of the usurpation with the help of a third party which is why I find the propect of having a sidereal in the game useful as both a plot device and an interesting character.<br /> <br /> I'm not exactly sure at which time the game would take place in the timeline of creation. I want the players to have time to build a powerbase and actually begin to fight the bad guys avengers style if you get what I mean. I was thinking of using denandsor or rathess as the stage for the game. I think both have interesting potential for all exalted type. I am not familiar with sidereal charms and astrology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 03-14-2015, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:10:46-07:00","id":440886,"title":"","content":"No worries. As I mentioned before, I really shouldn't be picking up another play by post game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:14:53-07:00","id":440889,"title":"","content":"Then why talk to me about it then ? How many games are you in ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:17:56-07:00","id":440893,"title":"","content":"Just two. I mentioned because you ask and it was a case of &quot;The odds of me ever playing this character as slim to nil, so if I find a game that it could fit in, I'd better jump on it&quot;. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:23:44-07:00","id":440899,"title":"","content":"Sorry I'm a bit tired it's like 2 in the morning for me, but yeah I get the feeling I have a nice dawn caste made for a first age game but they are a rare thing to find. Thanks for showing interest though it's always welcomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T15:07:56-07:00","id":441870,"title":"","content":"It's okay. I didn't mean to lead you on. I've posted crazy stuff at 2 am before too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T17:59:57-07:00","id":442022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth?p=440849#post440849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like fun, how powerful were you guys at the beginning of the game? I've been toying with the idea of trying to ST a <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">more &quot;powered-up&quot; </span></span></span>game but I can't seem to come up with a good idea. That and some of my friends traumatized me about trying but I think I can handle it in play by post.</div> </div> </div> </div>E5 in both cases. The second one had us coming out of stasis centuries after we were supposed to, though we didn't know why. We had hopped to ride out the Userpation and return as most powerful solars in the world with our hidden manses as seeds to build a more perfect Creation. (Our Sid player was actually manipulating us by making it look like a DB thing and not a Sid backing DB thing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T19:34:52-07:00","id":442094,"title":"","content":"if anyone is interested in running it, though, I'd be down to play in an Elder/First Age game. That sounds interesting as all heck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T08:21:22-07:00","id":442558,"title":"","content":"I've tried to run one once before.<br /> <br /> Didn't work out very well, mostly because the scale was all wonky. If I was gonna try it again, I'd try to keep it localized: a newly Exalted Solar PC and their lieutenants and hangers-on (Lunar mate, Dragonblooded lieutenants, Sidereal advisor, etc) managing an established (likely inherited) domain. Lots of finding out about skeletons in the previous administration's (slash previous incarnation's) closet, lots of trying to protect your little city-state from the threat of Deliberative politics and the whims of your neighbors.<br /> <br /> In my experience, the easy travel and communication and high power level of First Age games tends to make them too diffuse too fast. PCs tend to get scattered, STs have a whole lot more work because fast communication and global politics means you need to juggle the entire setting instead of just building up the believability of your local region first (you have to figure out what power players on the other side of Creation think about the PCs' actions, because they'll actually <i>hear</i> about them, unlike in Time of Tumult Creation).. Storytelling tends to end up spread too thin, and the whole thing tends to fall apart.<br /> <br /> To avoid those pitfalls, I'd run it as a family-style game. The PCs should all be closely and intimately connected to one another, and should all have strong ties and attachments to a particular locale. I'd try to keep power levels reasonably low rather than letting anyone play Elders if it was a First Age game, especially in 2E: too many &quot;I resolve the entire plot&quot; charms sitting around at high Essence. I'd try to convey that sense of power through infrastructure instead: the PCs literally run the place they're in, and their orders have the weight of law. It's all about protecting and managing your home base, and nearby city states and their Exalted lords are your antagonists.<br /> <br /> ...I'm not offering to run a First Age game, I don't have the time to commit to it. But if any of y'all want to try it, that's my advice: keep it local, keep the PCs tight as family, and keep the PCs power level pretty low so they can actually do things instead of spending motes to solve all their problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:40:53-07:00","id":446848,"title":"","content":"Ah, thanks, Guru. Oh well. So much for not being a ST.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I'm back, and I updated! Sorry for the late update, my work is working me to the bone. Again.<br /> <br /> @Exthalion: Are you talking to master Ironsong there? Just for clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:47:57-07:00","id":446852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth?p=446848#post446848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, thanks, Guru. Oh well. So much for not being a ST.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I'm back, and I updated! Sorry for the late update, my work is working me to the bone. Again.<br /> <br /> @Exthalion: Are you talking to master Ironsong there? Just for clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am. (Necessary words)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:51:39-07:00","id":446875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=446845#post446845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Prodigal Marian)<br /> <br /> The cause of death was simple: the back half of the animal in question was missing. What it was, though, was another kettle of fish entirely. It was about the size of a dog, with fuzzy feathers, and a small, beady eyes. A beak suggested it being a bird, but the one attached limb had a hoof at the end of its limb. Curious.<br /> <br /> On the body, though, was a message in Old Realm who had a definite anachronistic twang to it. Not the harsh syllables of Malfeas or the flowy script of Heaven. No, this is clear, concise and almost blocky.<br /> <br /> &quot;I have been called. You forget. I will feast on your bones in one moon's passing. THE KING OF HOOF,&quot; it reads.<br /> <br /> What will you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops. I wonder if Mastery of Small Matters works on primordial creatures. :-O<br /> <br /> <br /> This might be the best copy and paste error ever! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-17-2015, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T19:41:03-07:00","id":446921,"title":"","content":"Let's hope that doesn't get us into trouble <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:06:42-07:00","id":446972,"title":"","content":"Blah. Getting into trouble gives us something to do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T06:41:39-07:00","id":447635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=446918#post446918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unrestrained Lover chuckle at the mention of automaton yet the tone of his voice remain calm even amused a bit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">&quot;Please call me Eisen, I do have a proposal in mind you are a sharp one Mr. Zan. My companion and I wish to explore the labyrinth, we require a guide and you seem to be the one for the job in exchange for your expertise and time I will arm you and your hunting companion with advanced weapons and gear some will be simply mechanical but other can be much more powerful and if you ask how powerful well... You can see for yourself.</span><br /> <br /> True to his word unrestrained Lover lift his right arm puling back his sleeve to reveal the bronze like flesh of his forearm covered in intricate motonic circuits and metal plates. Before anyone can say anything his arm split open into four parts revealing the turning gears and piston inside it, his hand is pulled inside as the four part of his forearm extend other metal plates to connect to one another creating a large cylinder from which a cannon barrel extend instead of a hand. Taking aim at a lonely chair in the tavern a few yards away from their table the cannon begins to rotate becoming faster until it turn at several rotation per second before spitting a fiery ball of blue plasma in a thunderous boom that desintegrate most of the chair as steam vents from small tubes near his elbow before his arm retake it's original appearance. (Unrestrained Lover spends 6 motes of personnal essence: 5 to deploy the pulse cannon and one to fire)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">&quot;Is that enough to impress you ?&quot;</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Magnusar, did the Unrestrained Lover use that demonstration with the Haslanti League?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:03:32-07:00","id":447647,"title":"","content":"No he but he demonstrated an advanced knowledge of magitech and gave them pointers how to build the heat engine of their flying ships. (I understand from the book that they have trouble to reverse engineer them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T18:19:30-07:00","id":448580,"title":"","content":"Argh, my typing these last couple posts is absolutely bollocks. Apologies all-round. I'll try to proof-read better. I suppose this is also due to me re-wording things part-way through, and not redoing the rest of that sentence. <br /> <br /> Anyways, Guru, I'm now imagining Nergui as a sort of unwitting messiah. His actions are an interesting foil to Merciful, and this is producing a good dynamic. Merciful is creating a cult of personality for his own selfish goals, while Nergui may get one due to his simple thought processes, kind actions, and the Haslanti League viewing Lunars as culture heroes and god-beasts of beneficience from their origins.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T18:23:18-07:00","id":448584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth?p=447647#post447647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No he but he demonstrated an advanced knowledge of magitech and gave them pointers how to build the heat engine of their flying ships. (I understand from the book that they have trouble to reverse engineer them)</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that while they're costly to produce and maintain, the average dirigible airship is easy enough to create. It's the Final Fantasy-esque spaceships with gas bags that can fly to the moon, are powered by crystals and have magical bunks that heal all injuries that the Haslans cannot reproduce, but I'm sure Bright Shattered Ice's endless city of fun has provided them with a few of those as wrecks and crashed hulks.<br /> <br /> In case you don't get it, I think Tzitzli is probably my favorite place from Dreams of the First Age. Fuck year, giant floating paradise city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T20:14:25-07:00","id":448733,"title":"","content":"Well, FFVI had the dirigibles. FFIV style rotor-lift Airships could be do-able. Of course, since I passed on playing an Abyssal version of the Lord Captain of the Red Wings, I won't push for that style of ship. Howl, using Necrotech I could have a ship that flies even though it doesn't have any apparent means of generating lift. Just rambling here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T20:27:29-07:00","id":448746,"title":"","content":"Belkra, what do we call your character? Prodigal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T07:00:20-07:00","id":449154,"title":"","content":"I also thought we kind of knew Belkra's character from the airship (not that he mentioned that he was an Abyssal). We probably would have noticed strange underworld vibes before this. Is he doing something extra Abyssal-like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T09:32:07-07:00","id":449371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth?p=449154#post449154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also thought we kind of knew Belkra's character from the airship (not that he mentioned that he was an Abyssal). We probably would have noticed strange underworld vibes before this. Is he doing something extra Abyssal-like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did we? I thought he arrived a different way since Belkra himself started a bit late. If that's the case, I can edit it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T09:36:30-07:00","id":449375,"title":"","content":"I think it was decided that he hung out on the Airship for a bit after the rest of us left. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth?p=427346#post427346\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/g...346#post427346</a><br /> <br /> There is a lot of characters, so it is a bit confusing who met who where. I think the only character that did not come on the airship is Xisa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T13:32:41-07:00","id":449700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth?p=449375#post449375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was decided that he hung out on the Airship for a bit after the rest of us left. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth?p=427346#post427346\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/g...346#post427346</a><br /> <br /> There is a lot of characters, so it is a bit confusing who met who where. I think the only character that did not come on the airship is Xisa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'll fix that when I get home from work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:39:57-07:00","id":451105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth?p=448733#post448733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, FFVI had the dirigibles. FFIV style rotor-lift Airships could be do-able. Of course, since I passed on playing an Abyssal version of the Lord Captain of the Red Wings, I won't push for that style of ship. Howl, using Necrotech I could have a ship that flies even though it doesn't have any apparent means of generating lift. Just rambling here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, I was thinking FF4's Big Whale when I wrote that. That and the Grand Ship in Bravely Default. Another good game.<br /> <br /> Prodigal could have a ship powered by a dead god of wind, a ship propelled by the unanswered prayers of orphans, or hell, even one empowered by Oblivion which obliterates gravity's effect on it. <br /> <br /> Now that I think on it, it's probably for the best that I've never really played a loyalist Deathknight. I'd probably get really into the whole over the top death aspects and the whole thing would become a really, really sardonically black comedy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T19:55:28-07:00","id":451202,"title":"","content":"@wonderandawe: It doesn't matter to him what you call him. Prodigal, Marian, Hey you, Hey Jude, it's all good. No, he isn't doing anything extra Abyssal-y. Of course, he has one howl of a killer thirst, if you know what I am talking about. He expended essence and the best way to get it back is to have a nice, warm drink...<br /> <br /> Should anyone have directly asked the question, Prodigal would have admitted to being Exalted in the Black fashion, by whom and for what purpose, he won't say. He will only allude to being on the run from a very powerful personage in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> @Dietaku: Yep, I was thinking Lunar Whale, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":1146,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","user":"Belkra","date":". 07-06-2019, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T15:02:52-07:00","id":452039,"title":"","content":"Damn! Orca has four resources! I know who bank rolling this expedition! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title